<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="66764f89">Any member of the team can identify project risks at any time; however, it is best to review the risks as part of
regular project control meetings and to have someone designated to maintain version control over the register.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b266c9a7"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="8165412f"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="3faacbe8">&lt;p&gt;
    A risk is a possible event that has not yet occurred. It typically can have a negative impact and should be managed to
    prevent the project from going off track in the future. A risk unmanaged, accepted, or not fully mitigated usually
    becomes an issue.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Risk should be examined through various dimensions, such as strategic, operational, financial, regulatory,
    reputational, technical and others.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
